# Line endings (cadence.md §7.14, TD-187): every text file is LF in the repository and in every
# checkout, whatever a clone's core.autocrlf says. A file that must be CRLF says so below.
# agent-cadence's own copy of its seed (files/.gitattributes): keep the two the same.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows scripts, run by cmd.exe or PowerShell, keep CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# This repo's own patterns, below the seed's (test_adopt.sh holds the lines above to files/.gitattributes).
# ledgerboard's fixtures, byte for byte, never converted (TD-213): some are CRLF on purpose, inputs read
# exactly as written, and tests/ledgerboard.MANIFEST hashes each. (The package itself, files/scripts/ledgerboard/,
# is LF throughout, so files/.gitattributes' LF rule leaves its bytes, and its release hashes, as they are.)
tests/ledgerboard/** -text
